# content/ is the database, and two different programs write it: the PHP API running on
# Linux and the Python tools running on Windows. Both emit LF.
#
# Without this, git converts to CRLF on checkout on Windows, and then every byte-identical
# comparison fails: tools/import_concepts.py would see all 208 concepts as "updated" on a
# fresh clone and rewrite files nothing had changed. Normalising to LF everywhere keeps
# `git status` meaningful.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
